    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gummi</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cummi</span></b> , indecl.
		n., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-mis</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cummis</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gummis</span></b> , is, f. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> Graec.
			gummeos, <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, §
			225</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμμι</span>, <i>gum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 26, 45, § 108</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">24, 1, 1, §
				3 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 12,
				26, § 66</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				52, 16</span></i> et saep. (in Plin. cummi or cummis is the reading
			in the best MSS.).</div>
